     treatment: 'Non-meningeal disease: high-dose amoxicillin first-line for susceptible/low-level resistant strains (Grade A); ceftriaxone for severe/hospitalised disease. Meningitis: empirical ceftriaxone PLUS vancomycin until susceptibility confirmed, given the risk of penicillin-non-susceptible <i>Streptococcus pneumoniae</i> in the CNS compartment (Grade A) — adjunctive dexamethasone reduces neurological complications. Vaccination (PCV/PPSV23) is the primary prevention strategy.',
